  "id": "rayleigh-plesset-bubble-third-science",
  "name": "Rayleigh-Plesset gas-bubble oscillation and viscous energy loss",
  "description": "Spherical gas compression, radial fluid inertia, surface tension and viscous damping. Incompressible unbounded liquid and uniform polytropic gas; this small oscillation does not model violent collapse, heat/mass transfer or sonoluminescence. Illustrative millimetre bubble with water-like rho1000,mu0.001,surface tension0.072 SI; ambient100kPa,gas reference100144Pa,exponent1.4,initial radius1.05mm,speed0. Horizon3ms,RK4step0.5microsecond. No vapor pressure or gas diffusion. Original mathematical transcription/adaptation; not a calibrated forecast. Signed net-rate flows implement the stated equations. No numerical clamps or hidden resets.",
  "category": "physics",
  "source": "https://media.library.caltech.edu/CaltechBOOK:1995.001/chap2.htm",
  "reference": "Brennen (1995), Cavitation and Bubble Dynamics, Chapter2, Rayleigh-Plesset equation and bubble-gas closure; polytropic gas specialization.",
